I logged in this morning and came to a fresh new day of Nethack. I
found some eggs and a food ration or two in an icebox, and ate them to
satiate myself. Walking outside, I found that there was an abundance of
trees, and very few monsters. Perhaps this is a bones level? I
navagated through the passages of the maze. Some seemed to be wider and
different than others, which is unusual, but there's always new things
in Nethack.

Eventually I found a large dog, and I tamed it with a meatball I'd
brought along with me, but a @ came up and shouted at me. Since he was
still mostly peaceful, I walked away to prevent evoking an alignment
penalty. The next dog I saw was hostile, and I was out of treats. I
found that I'd left my weapons in my stash, and all I had on was a +0
T-Shirt. Still, I was able to punch it to death, though sustaining a
bit of damage myself. For some reason the nearby @ were disturbed, but
maybe they were just woken up by the combat.

I wandered into an area with lots of stores, and decided to browse. I
found that one store had a massive collection magic markers! Just my
luck! I bought a huge load of them, some blank scrolls, and some
spellbooks, with some zorkmids to spare. The other @ stared at me like
I was crazy, but then again, my charisma wasn't too high. I found some
walking shoes and a cloth helm in another store, and picked out some
more T-Shirts with collectable messages that the shopkeeper assured me
were enchanted to +3. For some reason he got mad when I tried to try
one on in front of him, so I ditched the new clothes and walked out.

Then I saw this temple nearby and found that it had a priest. Since I
had some zorkmids with me, I donated some money to the priest, but my
AC didn't lower! After giving all of my money to him (and I could sense
that he was getting impatient each time I donated) and still not
getting any results, I decided to give him a whack on the head and take
back my money. Bad move -- it seems that I was in a town, and the watch
came and locked me up after some nearby @'s screamed and alerted them.

So here I am, in this little cell, with no way out: the door's locked,
the watch took my key, and I seem to have forgotten the knock spell -
it's just not working! Trying to use charm monster on the guard has no
beneficial effects, though I got a few YAFMs. I lost my telepathy when
I murdered the priest, so I can't even look outside for entertainment.
At least food isn't an issue - they send in what must be C- or
K-rations, the food's so bland.

The only identified wand I have is a wand of cold, and it seems to be
out of charges. I've tried engrave-testing my maple and oak wands, but
they don't have any effect; none of them is a /oOpening either. All of
my scrolls are blank, and reading them has no effect. I have two
spellbooks with me, but neither is identified. One is labeled "King
Lear", and the other one is labeled "The Canterbury Tales", but the
mystical runes were just too much to comprehend.

I think this game is a dead end, but the scariest thing is, I don't
seem to be able to exit out of the game. Good thing I installed the
Suicide Patch....



